<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CLOUD COVER</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 08:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (NOMADS)<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t00z-tcdc-anl<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 09:23 PM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (hourly HRRR cycle, 15-min steps)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover/legend.png?v=hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t00z-tcdc-anl" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Cloud cover (%, as filed by HRRR): <b>LOWEST 0 clear</b> transparent &rarr; thin cloud <b>dark-blue/blue/cyan</b> &rarr; <b>40 green</b> &rarr; <b>55 yellow</b> &rarr; <b>70 orange</b> &rarr; <b>82 red</b> &rarr; <b>90 magenta</b> &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100 overcast</b> dark-purple. Same % always shows the same color; clear areas stay see-through.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km TCDC total cloud cover, entire-atmosphere analysis (hourly cycles + 15-min subhourly steps)<br/><a href="https://rapidrefresh.noaa.gov/hrrr">https://rapidrefresh.noaa.gov/hrrr</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE CLOUD COVER</h2><p>Hourly HRRR cloud analysis: how much of the sky over the Great Lakes basin is cloud-covered right now, in percent as filed by NOAA. Clear areas are transparent so the map underneath shows through.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover/legend.png?v=hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t00z-tcdc-anl" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Cloud cover (%, as filed by HRRR): <b>LOWEST 0 clear</b> transparent &rarr; thin cloud <b>dark-blue/blue/cyan</b> &rarr; <b>40 green</b> &rarr; <b>55 yellow</b> &rarr; <b>70 orange</b> &rarr; <b>82 red</b> &rarr; <b>90 magenta</b> &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100 overcast</b> dark-purple. Same % always shows the same color; clear areas stay see-through.</p><p><b>Units:</b> % cloud cover<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km TCDC total cloud cover, entire-atmosphere analysis (hourly cycles + 15-min subhourly steps)<br/><b>Update:</b> HRRR hourly cycles (15-min steps feed the hourly view)<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 08:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t00z-tcdc-anl<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 09:23 PM EDT<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://rapidrefresh.noaa.gov/hrrr">NOAA HRRR</a></p>]]></description>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
        <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover/current.png?v=hrrr-hrrr.20260926-t00z-tcdc-anl</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>900</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>49.5</north>
          <south>40.5</south>
          <east>-73.5</east>
          <west>-93.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
